{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1159236-2e-ally-from-american-horror-story-cult-is-good-fairest-example","id":1159236,"title":"[2E] Ally from American Horror Story: Cult is good Fairest example?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-11-15T15:49:37-08:00","id":1159236,"title":"[2E] Ally from American Horror Story: Cult is good Fairest example?","content":"It's a minor spoiler for the season finale, but it's heart of the topic. So if you watch <b>AHS: Cult</b> - just see 'Great Again' episode right now, it's worth it...<br /> <br /> <br /> Ended? Let's go for discussion. <a href=\"http://americanhorrorstory.wikia.com/wiki/Ally_Mayfair-Richards\" target=\"_blank\">Ally</a> is character that starts <i>very</i> broken in the season. She has kind heart, but is overburdened with her weakness. But the horrible situation of the season - like trauma of the Durance - has shuttered her so much, she needed to rebuild herself. So she become good. No, she become <i>perfect</i>. And she want's to lead. She also do some very <i>nasty</i> things just too make possible her leadership. At the end, we do not see that much difference between her - and her like-Keeper Kai Anderson. Thing that was marking of 1E Fairest was they acted many times like Gentry and that many Losts pointed there is not very much difference between two.<br /> <br /> In 2E Fairest seems to still working as 'good guys', but in my mind Ally would be perfect example how it should work. So is it place for characters like her in new take on Fairest Seeming from 2E?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T17:56:47-08:00","id":1160065,"title":"","content":"Yes<br /> <br /> Apparently I need at least 10 characters so: Yes very much yes. In fact I had Fairest in mind while powerwatching the season this wednesday. (haven't yet seen the finale but I can more or less tell where it's going). But yea, tottally an awesome Fairest aimed story. Changeling in general with how much it deals with Trauma and how different people deal with it. <br /> <br /> So much of the season shows different kinds of abuse, especcially the massive Greenlighting from the first few eps. You get:<br /> - Fairest characters like Kai and Ally<br /> - Darklings like Winter and Valerie (and mybe Ivy?)<br /> - Wizened like Vincent, and Ivy<br /> - Elementals like Ivy, and Bebe<br /> - Ogres like Harrison, Beverly, Gary, and Bebe (kinda fits both)<br /> - Beasts like Jack Samuels, Meadow<br /> <br /> I'm sure I can think of others but those are who I think about and it's not super perfect (hard to pin down Ivy, her throwing herself at her work (very Wizened), her distancing from reality (very elemental), her tendency to metaphorically hide from problems (very darkling)) but still.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T07:19:50-08:00","id":1160204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1159236-2e-ally-from-american-horror-story-cult-is-good-fairest-example?p=1160065#post1160065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Darklings like Winter and Valerie (and mybe Ivy?)</div> </div> </div> </div>How do you see this 'isolation' in those characters that 2E corebook points too?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1159236-2e-ally-from-american-horror-story-cult-is-good-fairest-example?p=1160065#post1160065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Elementals like Ivy, and Bebe</div> </div> </div> </div>Why should those be Elementals?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T15:06:00-08:00","id":1160322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1159236-2e-ally-from-american-horror-story-cult-is-good-fairest-example?p=1160204#post1160204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How do you see this 'isolation' in those characters that 2E corebook points too?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Why should those be Elementals?</div> </div> </div> </div>How I read the seeming from 2nd ed so far, each seeming seems to be a halfway point between a fairytale character archetype and a generalization of a coping mechanism for trauma.<br /> <br /> The way I read them (though they are a bit vague and can fit a few different one)<br /> - beasts cope by deciding not to care about rules or anything but their will (they just got it back)<br /> - fairest cope by turning their control outwards on others<br /> - elementals cope by, essentially, checking out (with different flavored per chosen element)<br /> - Ogres cope by turning inwards, doing what they can, almost as if they feel they have to atone (this one is a little scratchy, there's a few interpretations from the text)<br /> - wizened cope by throwing themselves at their work, hobbies and otherwise (this one was crystal clear)<br /> - darklings cope by retreating from attention and keeping secrets and knowing what they can.<br /> <br /> Winter struck me as a darkling first because of the thing she said to Ivy (I think). Something like &quot;the only thing I want now is to stand in the shadows helping a great person be greater&quot;. That and the amount of roles/masks she plays.<br /> <br /> We didn't see much of Valerie but I saw it very similar. Not the kind to be upfront but to share the right thing at the right time only &quot;trusting&quot; a select few if even then.<br /> <br /> Ivy was a stretch. Mostly how she felt with her wife. <br /> <br /> As far as elemental: both Ivy and Bebe seemed to be almost a force of nature like how the book described. There was never a time that either *didn't* do a thing and something happened. <br /> <br /> Still tho there's some oddness with it. Like there's a few that seem to become dependent and Ogres have a touch of that so winter could be an Ogre. <br /> <br /> But any that's how I came up with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}